ex:Circuit_Breaker a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Circuit Breaker" ;
    rdfs:comment "A circuit breaker is a safety device to prevent damage to devices in a circuit, such as electric motors, and wiring when the current flowing through the electrical circuit supersedes its design limits. It does this by removing the current from a circuit when an unsafe condition arises. Unlike a switch, a circuit breaker automatically does this and shuts off the power immediately." ;
